WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:05.100
Jared Leto reportedly had trouble putting
on a happy face when hearing about the new

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.120
Joker movie.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:11.460
According to a story published by The Hollywood
Reporter detailing how former Joker producer

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:15.800
Martin Scorsese may have contributed to the
film after dropping his producing credit,

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:21.500
Jared Leto who played the Joker in 2016's
Suicide Squad was none too pleased about studio

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:26.620
Warner Bros. moving forward with the Joker
origin story film starring Joaquin Phoenix.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:31.380
Reportedly, Leto was left feeling out in the
cold when former Warner Bros. president Kevin

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:36.500
Tsujihara and current studio chief Toby Emmerich
decided to give the project the greenlight.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:40.640
Emmerich is said to have, quote, "loved the
script" that Phillips co-wrote with Academy

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:45.180
Award-nominated screenwriter Scott Silver,
though he did reportedly feel that the gritty

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:50.050
nature of the story might fit better outside
of the standard DC Extended Universe, of which

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.840
Suicide Squad is a part.

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:57.280
Nonetheless, Emmerich was taken with Joker,
as was Tsujihara, and the rest is history.

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:02.400
Neither Leto nor any representatives of his
have come forward to confirm or deny the claim

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.640
that he was hurt over the Phoenix-led Joker,
but the actor's purported reaction to hearing

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:11.740
the news of the project getting the greenlight
may be accurate given past Joker-related events.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:17.520
As fans know, Leto's Joker didn't have nearly
as prominent a role in Suicide Squad as expected.

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:22.580
His involvement essentially amounted to an
extended cameo rather than a starring part,

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:25.970
which left audiences and Leto disappointed
and confused.

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:27.880
"Oh, I'm not gonna kill ya.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:34.860
I'm just gonna hurt ya — really, really
bad."

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:39.310
Director David Ayer even admitted that he
should have included more of Leto's Joker

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:39.940
in the film.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.680
In an open letter published in January 2017,
Ayer wrote:

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:45.560
"Wish I had a time machine.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:49.120
I'd make Joker the main villain and engineer
a more grounded story.

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:51.800
I have to take the good and bad and learn
from it."

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:57.180
That considered, one can easily see how Leto
may have felt alienated and upset when Warner

00:01:57.190 --> 00:02:01.380
Bros. chose to go ahead with Phillips and
Phoenix's Joker movie, the idea for which

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:07.100
Phillips pitched to Warner Bros. in August
2016, the same month that Suicide Squad opened

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:07.800
in theaters.

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:12.560
Learning one year later that a different actor
would get the chance to play the Joker in

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:17.860
his very own solo movie very well might have
crushed Leto's spirits even if Warner Bros.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:21.560
executives emphasized that the project wouldn't
be the end of Leto's Joker.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:26.780
Shortly after Warner Bros. and DC Films made
the announcement about the Joker standalone

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:31.470
film, The Hollywood Reporter ran a piece noting
that Leto made sure his agents knew he wasn't

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:34.700
happy with the idea of multiple, competing
Jokers.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:39.260
Leto later told On Demand Entertainment that
he was, quote, "a little confused" about the

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:44.061
future plans for the Joker which, at the time,
included a spin-off movie featuring his Joker

00:02:44.061 --> 00:02:45.980
and Margot Robbie's Harley Quinn.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.020
However, he maintained a level head.

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:48.620
He admitted:

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:49.680
"I love the Joker.

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:52.620
He's a great character and really fun character
to play.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:56.660
But it's a big universe and when you play
the Joker, there's no ownership there.

00:02:56.820 --> 00:03:00.520
You have the honor of holding the baton for
a little while and then passing it off.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:04.780
There are other films that are in development
and I'm excited to see what comes from them."

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:06.820
"Are you sweet-talking me?

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:09.980
Ah hah hah."

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:15.720
Leto's disposition likely turned sunny in
June 2018, when it was reported that Warner

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:20.500
Bros. was developing a standalone Joker movie
featuring Leto's iteration of the infamous

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:21.720
DC Comics villain.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:26.620
The project, which Leto was also set to be
credited on as an executive producer, was

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:30.580
apparently intended to be the first of several
Suicide Squad off-shoots.

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:36.180
Unfortunately, it appears that both the Joker-Harley
Quinn spin-off film and the Joker solo flick

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:38.280
starring Leto have since been scrapped.

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:43.700
In February 2019, Forbes ran a piece noting
that both projects had, quote, "fallen by

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.320
the wayside" at Warner Bros.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:50.340
As of October 2019, we don't know for certain
what the future holds for Leto's Joker.

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:55.459
The easiest bet is that he could appear in
James Gunn's upcoming sequel-slash-reboot

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:59.740
The Suicide Squad, which features a mix of
returning characters and fresh faces.

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:03.920
There's been no formal announcement about
his possible involvement, though, so it's

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:08.420
a toss-up whether or not Leto will grace the
silver screen and flash Joker's silver teeth

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:10.620
in 2021's The Suicide Squad.

